# Normalise line endings to LF in the repo; check out as LF everywhere.
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true (set in Git for Windows' system gitconfig)
# gives fresh clones and new worktrees CRLF working-tree copies.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Rust: force text, and use git's built-in Rust hunk headers in diffs.
*.rs text eol=lf diff=rust
Cargo.toml text eol=lf
# Cargo.lock stays diffable on purpose: Cargo.toml holds only semver ranges,
# so the lockfile is the one place a resolved dependency bump shows up.
Cargo.lock text eol=lf

# Redundant under the baseline, and kept deliberately: in a shell script CRLF
# is fatal rather than untidy ("$'\r': command not found", "bad interpreter").
# If the baseline is ever loosened, this must not loosen with it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF. cmd.exe can miss goto/call labels in an
# LF-only batch file; PowerShell reads LF fine, and .ps1 follows the Windows
# convention.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries, such as a README screenshot. text=auto already detects most of
# them; `binary` makes it unconditional: no line-ending conversion, no text
# diff, no text merge.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.exe binary
